    ($SATQ$d139cf4b$SATQ$, $SATQ$581cd95e-37cf-4835-9e46-c492ec9a8f24$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is defined by the given equation. The function <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math> is defined by <math alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Which expression represents the maximum value of <math alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"16af1332-bc9b-4c39-b7df-b1c1a7cd3bfd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 plus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"7600d570-59eb-4fdd-8543-38f43300866a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"ec9ce01a-7643-4911-b72a-293bdd7b2666","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"7acc7c06-0410-4541-b9cb-447feb00e8cc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 minus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["7600d570-59eb-4fdd-8543-38f43300866a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that function&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g"><mi>g</mi></math> is defined by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="55 t minus 2 t squared"><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 t squared plus 55 t plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> can be found by completing the square to rewrite the equation defining&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g"><mi>g</mi></math> in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis t minus h right parenthesis squared plus k"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where the maximum value of the function is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math>, which occurs when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t equals h"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> is a negative constant. The equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 t squared plus 55 t plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t squared minus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction t right parenthesis plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, which can be rewritten as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t squared minus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction t plus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared right parenthesis plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t minus StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation is in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis t minus h right parenthesis squared plus k"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals negative 2"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h equals StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k equals 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.<br>Alternate approach: Since the function&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> is a quadratic function, the maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> occurs at the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> that&rsquo;s halfway between the two zeros of the function. The zeros of function&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> can be found by substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the equation defining <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math>, which yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0 equals 55 t minus 2 t squared"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0 equals t left parenthesis 55 minus 2 t right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. By the zero product property, it follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t equals 0"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="55 minus 2 t equals 0"><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="55"><mn>55</mn></math> from each side of the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="55 minus 2 t equals 0"><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="minus 2 t equals negative 55"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>55</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 2"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t equals StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the zeros of function&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. The value that&rsquo;s halfway between <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> can be found by calculating the average of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, which is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartStartFraction 0 plus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction OverOver 2 EndEndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. It follows that the maximum of function&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> occurs when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t equals StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> in the equation defining function&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 55 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 EndFraction minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>. Multiplying <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 EndFraction"><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="four fourths"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> in this equation to get a common denominator yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 4 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Since the equation defining <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, the maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> greater than the maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. It follows that the maximum value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"d139cf4b","external_id":"581cd95e-37cf-4835-9e46-c492ec9a8f24","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"519ae0df-b6da-4b2e-833f-edfe8ac51116","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by the given equation. The function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Which expression represents the maximum value of <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"16af1332-bc9b-4c39-b7df-b1c1a7cd3bfd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 plus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"7600d570-59eb-4fdd-8543-38f43300866a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"ec9ce01a-7643-4911-b72a-293bdd7b2666","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"7acc7c06-0410-4541-b9cb-447feb00e8cc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 minus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"}],"keys":["7600d570-59eb-4fdd-8543-38f43300866a"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi></math> is defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 t squared plus 55 t plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> can be found by completing the square to rewrite the equation defining&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi></math> in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis t minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where the maximum value of the function is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, which occurs when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals h\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is a negative constant. The equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 t squared plus 55 t plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t squared minus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, which can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t squared minus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction t plus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared right parenthesis plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t minus StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation is in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis t minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals negative 2\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.<br>Alternate approach: Since the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is a quadratic function, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> occurs at the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> that&rsquo;s halfway between the two zeros of the function. The zeros of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> can be found by substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the equation defining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math>, which yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0 equals 55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0 equals t left parenthesis 55 minus 2 t right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. By the zero product property, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals 0\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55 minus 2 t equals 0\"><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn></math> from each side of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55 minus 2 t equals 0\"><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 2 t equals negative 55\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>55</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 2\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the zeros of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. The value that&rsquo;s halfway between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> can be found by calculating the average of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, which is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartStartFraction 0 plus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction OverOver 2 EndEndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. It follows that the maximum of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> occurs when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> in the equation defining function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 55 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 EndFraction minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>. Multiplying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"four fourths\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> in this equation to get a common denominator yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 4 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Since the equation defining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> greater than the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. It follows that the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017718,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"d139cf4b","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1755117017718,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"581cd95e-37cf-4835-9e46-c492ec9a8f24","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"519ae0df-b6da-4b2e-833f-edfe8ac51116","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by the given equation. The function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Which expression represents the maximum value of <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>?</p>","keys":["7600d570-59eb-4fdd-8543-38f43300866a"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"16af1332-bc9b-4c39-b7df-b1c1a7cd3bfd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 plus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"7600d570-59eb-4fdd-8543-38f43300866a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"ec9ce01a-7643-4911-b72a-293bdd7b2666","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"7acc7c06-0410-4541-b9cb-447feb00e8cc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 minus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi></math> is defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 55 t minus 2 t squared plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 t squared plus 55 t plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> can be found by completing the square to rewrite the equation defining&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi></math> in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis t minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where the maximum value of the function is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, which occurs when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals h\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is a negative constant. The equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 t squared plus 55 t plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t squared minus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, which can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t squared minus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction t plus left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared right parenthesis plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals minus 2 left parenthesis t minus StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared plus 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation is in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis t minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals negative 2\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.<br>Alternate approach: Since the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is a quadratic function, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> occurs at the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> that&rsquo;s halfway between the two zeros of the function. The zeros of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> can be found by substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the equation defining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math>, which yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0 equals 55 t minus 2 t squared\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0 equals t left parenthesis 55 minus 2 t right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. By the zero product property, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals 0\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55 minus 2 t equals 0\"><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn></math> from each side of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"55 minus 2 t equals 0\"><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 2 t equals negative 55\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>55</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 2\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the zeros of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. The value that&rsquo;s halfway between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> can be found by calculating the average of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, which is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartStartFraction 0 plus StartFraction 55 Over 2 EndFraction OverOver 2 EndEndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. It follows that the maximum of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> occurs when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> in the equation defining function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 55 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 EndFraction minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>. Multiplying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"four fourths\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> in this equation to get a common denominator yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 4 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis minus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 squared Over 4 squared EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis equals 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Since the equation defining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis t right parenthesis plus 3\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> greater than the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. It follows that the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"g left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 plus 2 left parenthesis StartFraction 55 Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>55</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"581cd95e-37cf-4835-9e46-c492ec9a8f24","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1755117017718,"updateDate":1755117017718}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017718, 175511701