 a curve in the x y plane, with the origin labeled O. The numbers negative 8, negative 4, 4, and 8 are indicated on each axis. There are horizontal gridlines at the numbers negative 8 through 8, in increments of 2, on the y axis, and there are vertical gridlines at the numbers negative 8 through 8, in increments of 2, on the x axis. The figure presents an upward opening parabola, whose vertex lies at 4 on the x axis. The parabola passes through the point with coordinates 2 comma 4, and the point with coordinates 6 comma 4.\" width=\"114\" height=\"118\"><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;<img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d46da42c/img_003_3f947019.png\" alt=\"The answer choice presents the graph of a curve in the x y plane, with the origin labeled O. The numbers negative 8, negative 4, 4, and 8 are indicated on each axis. There are horizontal gridlines at the numbers negative 8 through 8, in increments of 2, on the y axis, and there are vertical gridlines at the numbers negative 8 through 8, in increments of 2, on the x axis. The figure presents an upward opening parabola, whose vertex lies at 4 on the y axis. The parabola passes through the point with coordinates negative 2 comma 8, and the point with coordinates 2 comma 8.\" width=\"114\" height=\"118\"><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. For the quadratic function <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d46da42c/img_006_255aaf58.png" alt="f of x equals, x squared, plus 4"></span>, the vertex of the graph is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d46da42c/img_007_7bed07dd.png" 