$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In the expression above, <span class="italic">b</span> and <span class="italic">c</span> are positive integers. If the expression is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_001_01de476c.png" alt="x plus b "></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_002_f96fc352.png" alt="x is not equal to b"></span>, which of the following could be the value of <span class="italic">c </span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">8</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">10</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. If the given expression is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_003_01de476c.png" alt="x plus b"></span>, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_004_ac1535ec.png" alt="the fraction with numerator x squared, minus c, and denominator x minus b, end fraction, equals, x plus b"></span>, where <span class="italic">x</span> isn&rsquo;t equal to <span class="italic">b</span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_005_b0e0741c.png" alt="x  minus b "></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_006_e3fa6eeb.png" alt="x squared, minus c, equals, open parenthesis, x plus b, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x minus b, close parenthesis"></span>. Since the right-hand side of this equation is in factored form for the difference of squares, the value of <span class="italic">c</span> must be a perfect square. Only choice A gives a perfect square for the value of <span class="italic">c</span>.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect. None of these values of <span class="italic">c</span> produces a difference of squares. For example, when 6 is substituted for <span class="italic">c</span> in the given expression, the result is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_007_cf2e12e1.png" alt="the fraction with numerator x squared, minus 6, and denominator x minus b, end fraction"></span>. The expression <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_008_bf9f5e22.png" alt="x squared, minus 6 "></span> can&rsquo;t be factored with integer values, and therefore <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_009_cf2e12e1.png" alt="the fraction with numerator x squared, minus 6, and denominator x minus b, end fraction "></span> isn&rsquo;t equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_010_01de476c.png" alt="x plus b"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
