c/img_007_cf2e12e1.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x squared, minus 6, and denominator x minus b, end fraction\"></span>. The expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_008_bf9f5e22.png\" alt=\"x squared, minus 6 \"></span> can&rsquo;t be factored with integer values, and therefore <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_009_cf2e12e1.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x squared, minus 6, and denominator x minus b, end fraction \"></span> isn&rsquo;t equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d8789a4c/img_010_01de476c.png\" alt=\"x plus b\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":11,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959623,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"d8789a4c","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1691007959623,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"028934-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"33f9cecc-f6c4-432b-9b5b-995c8c45aae1","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"028934-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x squared, minus c, and denominator x minus b, end fraction\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the expression above, <span class=\"italic\">b</span> and <span class=\"italic\">c</span> are positive integers. If the expression is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus b \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is not equal to b\"></span>, which of the following could be the value of <span class=\"italic\">c </span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">8</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">10</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. If the given expression is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus b\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x squared, minus c, and denominator x minus b, end fraction, equals, x plus b\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">x</span> isn&rsquo;t equal to <span class=\"italic\">b</span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x  minus b \"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared, minus c, equals, open parenthesis, x plus b, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x minus b, close parenthesis\"></span>. Since the right-hand side of this equation is in factored form for the difference of squares, the value of <span class=\"italic\">c</span> must be a perfect square. Only choice A gives a perfect square for the value of <span class=\"italic\">c</span>.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect. None of these values of <span class=\"italic\">c</span> produces a difference of squares. For example, when 6 is substituted for <span class=\"italic\">c</span> in the given expression, the result is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x squared, minus 6, and denominator x minus b, end fraction\"></span>. The expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared, minus 6 \"></span> can&rsquo;t be factored with integer values, and therefore <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x squared, minus 6, and denominator x minus b, end fraction \"></span> isn&rsquo;t equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus b\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959623,"updateDate":1691007959623}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959623, 1691007959623),
    ($SATQ$d8ace155$SATQ$, $SATQ$edb987d4-772f-4ea6-8b75-8cd93a8fc5c8$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$b45c5adf-318f-49fc-a5ec-df27ed8bdf28$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A company opens an account with an initial balance of <math alttext="dollar sign 36,100.00"><mo>$</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn>
</math>. The account earns interest, and no additional deposits or withdrawals are made. The account balance is given by an exponential function <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>, where <math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is the account balance, in dollars, <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> years after the account is opened. The account balance after <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> years is <math alttext="dollar sign 68,071.93"><mo>$</mo><mn>68,071.93</mn>
</math>. Which equation could define <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e283b70c-4d66-43f8-8604-dfb0e9ea7076","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 left parenthesis 1.05 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn>\n<msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1.05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"4b147c4e-4fb2-4bec-8166-eacb923260b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 31,971.93 left parenthesis 1.05 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>31,971.93</mn>\n<msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1.05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"efb5715f-51b6-482d-99fa-0faee040181c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 31,971.93 left parenthesis 0.05 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>31,971.93</mn>\n<msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"9937d872-7e88-4cfb-96f0-edbfed63f6bf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 left parenthesis 0.05 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn>\n<msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e283b70c-4d66-43f8-8604-dfb0e9ea7076"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. Since it's given that the account balance, <math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>, in dollars, after <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> years can be modeled by an exponential function, it follows that function <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> can be written in the form <math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals upper N r Superscript t"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></math>, where <math alttext="upper N"><mi>N</mi>
</math> is the initial value of the function and <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> is a constant related to the growth of the function. It's given that the initial balance of the account is <math alttext="dollar sign 36,100.00"><mo>$</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn></math>, so it follows that the initial value of the function, or <math alttext="upper N"><mi>N</mi>
</math>, must be&nbsp;<math alttext="36,100.00"><mn>36,100.00</mn></math>. Substituting&nbsp;<math alttext="36,100.00"><mn>36,100.00</mn></math> for <math alttext="upper N"><mi>N</mi>
</math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals upper N r Superscript t"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 r Superscript t"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></math>. It's given that the account balance after <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> years, or when <math alttext="t equals 13"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math>, is&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 68,071.93"><mo>$</mo><mn>68,071.93</mn></math>. It follows that <math alttext="upper A left parenthesis 13 right parenthesis equals 68,071.93"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mn>13</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>68,071.93</mn></math>, or <math alttext="36,100.00 r Superscript 13 Baseline equals 68,071.93"><mn>36,100.00</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>13</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>68,071.93</mn></math>. Dividing each side of the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="36,100.00 r Superscript 13 Baseline equals 68,071.93"><mn>36,100.00</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>13</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>68,071.93</mn></math> by&nbsp;<math alttext="36,100.00"><mn>36,100.00</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="r Superscript 13 Baseline equals StartFraction 68,071.93 Over 36,100.00 EndFraction"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>13</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>68,071.93</mn><mn>36,100.00</mn></mfrac></math>. Taking the <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math>th root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="r equals RootIndex 13 StartRoot StartFraction 68,071.93 Over 36,100.00 EndFraction EndRoot"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mroot><mfrac><mn>68,071.93</mn><mn>36,100.00</mn></mfrac><mn>13</mn></mroot></math>, or <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> is approximately equal to <math alttext="1.05"><mn>1.05</mn>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="1.05"><mn>1.05</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 r Superscript t"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 left parenthesis 1.05 right parenthesis Superscript t"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.05</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math>, so the equation <math alttext="upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 left parenthesis 1.05 right parenthesis Superscript t"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.05</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math> could define <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> in this function indicates an initial balance of <math alttext="dollar sign 31,971.93"><mo>$</mo><mn>31,971.93</mn></math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 36,100.00"><mo>$</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> in this function indicates an initial balance of <math alttext="dollar sign 31,971.93"><mo>$</mo><mn>31,971.93</mn></math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 36,100.00"><mo>$</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn></math>. Additionally, this function indicates the account balance is decreasing, rather than increasing, over time.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This function indicates the account balance is decreasing, rather than increasing, over time.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"d8ace155","external_id":"edb987d4-772f-4ea6-8b75-8cd93a8fc5c8","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"b45c5adf-318f-49fc-a5ec-df27ed8bdf28","uId":"be6a42a0-ee10-474c-8a87-9e7b0e254d11","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A company opens an account with an initial balance of <math alttext=\"dollar sign 36,100.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn>\n</math>. The account earns interest, and no additional deposits or withdrawals are made. The account balance is given by an exponential function <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is the account balance, in dollars, <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> years after the account is opened. The account balance after <math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math> years is <math alttext=\"dollar sign 68,071.93\"><mo>$</mo><mn>68,071.93</mn>\n</math>. Which equation could define <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e283b70c-4d66-43f8-8604-dfb0e9ea7076","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 36,100.00 left parenthesis 1.05 right parenthesis Superscript t\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36,100.00</mn>\n<msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1.05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"4b147c4e-4fb2-4bec-8166-eacb923260b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"upper A left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 31,971.93 left parenthesis 1.05 right paren