ath id=\"pcfc5de202d\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"262.488358\" x=\"9.200821\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>Moving from left to right:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve is in quadrant 1.</li>\n<li>From point (0 comma 9), the curve trends down sharply.</li>\n<li>From point (5 comma 1), the curve trends down gradually.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph gives the estimated number of catalogs <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, in thousands, a company sent to its customers at the end of each year, where <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represents the number of years since the end of <math alttext=\"1992\"><mn>1992</mn>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"0 less than or equals x less than or equals 10\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>10</mn></math>. Which statement is the best interpretation of the <em>y</em>-intercept in this context?</p>","externalid":"433ee68c-fedc-4334-84d7-4032b35bf0e2","templateid":"d10bb57d-d1b7-4f9f-906a-741f7d915608","vaultid":"a174acc8-d582-4865-bfab-572e5bfd64e9","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"541704c1-7a90-4632-a747-5bfba3dcde6f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated total number of catalogs the company sent to its customers during the first <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> years was <math alttext=\"9,000\"><mn>9,000</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"137a7915-9827-430e-810c-ed93fd82c162","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated total number of catalogs the company sent to its customers from the end of <math alttext=\"1992\"><mn>1992</mn>\n</math> to the end of <math alttext=\"2002\"><mn>2002</mn>\n</math> was <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"1ec3b392-0b0f-4aef-b643-5b8980691cad","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated number of catalogs the company sent to its customers at the end of <math alttext=\"1992\"><mn>1992</mn>\n</math> was <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"e0cf3489-1f2f-49d6-b060-9a79c1cac3aa","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated number of catalogs the company sent to its customers at the end of <math alttext=\"1992\"><mn>1992</mn>\n</math> was <math alttext=\"9,000\"><mn>9,000</mn>\n</math>.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1691007959826,"updateDate":1691007959826}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959826, 1691007959826),
    ($SATQ$dba7432e$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$017018-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference"><table class="table_WithBorder tcp-11178d0a-bbd6-4727-92cd-17135268ac70"><tbody><tr><td class="tcp-ca4d8494-78ff-4300-b848-3703b09287f9"><span class="italic"><span class="italic">x</span></span></td><td class="tcp-5b53cc14-8401-45b5-9507-66a4249218bd"><span class="italic"><span class="italic">f</span></span>(<span class="italic"><span class="italic">x</span></span>)</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-521d4d07-28b8-4daa-b77d-e0434944d475">0</td><td class="tcp-5dc6d263-bc4f-4730-b2e3-ca19d275c816">5</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-84c9dcf9-429a-4726-94c0-4107ab20e051">1</td><td class="tcp-88de162c-2093-4e1a-a8b1-65cd689a2425"><span class="math_expression "><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_004_35c68a84.png" alt="five halves"></span></span></span></td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-ee7c5afd-a559-4f13-a01c-ccfd49057622">2</td><td class="tcp-fa424496-8a6e-4daf-a749-150da6a81bbf"><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_005_132ee57b.png" alt="five fourths"></span></span></td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-ee7c1cf2-e55b-4101-855b-2ca4d512bb13">3</td><td class="tcp-77a8bb6e-6139-439b-afa5-e838babaac76"><span class="math_expression "><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_006_7e371ff9.png" alt="five eighths"></span></span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The table above gives the values of the function <span class="italic">f</span> for some values of <span class="italic">x</span>. Which of the following equations could define <span class="italic">f</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_000_d9879485.png\" alt=\"f of x equals, 5 times, open parenthesis, 2 raised to the x plus 1 power, close parenthesis\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_001_524334d6.png\" alt=\"f of x equals, 5 times, open parenthesis, 2 to the x power, close parenthesis\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_002_bc8747ba.png\" alt=\"f of x equals, 5 times, open parenthesis, 2 raised to the negative, open parenthesis, x plus 1, close parenthesis, power, close parenthesis\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_003_d503a936.png\" alt=\"f of x equals, 5 times, open parenthesis, 2 to the negative x power, close parenthesis\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. Each choice has a function with coefficient 5 and base 2, so the exponents must be analyzed. When the input value of <span class="italic">x</span> increases, the output value of <span class="italic">f</span>(<span class="italic">x</span>) decreases, so the exponent must be negative. An exponent of &ndash;<span class="italic">x</span> yields the values in the table: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_007_c1814633.png" alt="first value, 5, which equals 5 times open parenthesis, 2 to the negative 0 power, close parenthesis"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_008_b07485ed.png" alt="second value, five halves, which equals 5 times open parenthesis, 2 to the negative 1 power, close parenthesis"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_009_985f036d.png" alt="third value, five fourths, which equals 2 to the negative 2 power"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/dba7432e/img_010_96c05073.png" alt="fourth value, five eighths, which equals 5 times open parenthesis, 2 to the negative 3 power, close parenthesis"></span>.<p>Choices A and B are incorrect and may result from choosing equations that yield an increasing, rather than decreasing, output value of <span class="italic">f</span>(<span class="italic">x</span>) when the input value of <span class="italic">x</span> increases. Choice C is incorrect and may result from choosing an equation that doesn&rsquo;t yield the values in the table.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
